% 37 bars of 2/4. One motif (A D E F# | A . F# .) handed from instrument to instrument, one per way of painting:
% 1-3 cave: flute, frame drum · 4-5 Egypt: harp · 6-7 Greek vase: ukulele as a lyre · 8-9 mosaic: bell over a fifth
% 10-11 Song ink: dizi · 12-13 stained glass: glass over a pad · 14-15 Renaissance: guitar, violin · 16-17 ukiyo-e: guzheng
% 18-19 Impressionism: piano · 20-21 pointillism: pizzicato, glockenspiel · 22-24 Van Gogh: the strings
% 25-26 cubism: the motif knocked off the beat · 27-28 De Stijl: boogie-woogie · 29-30 cut-outs: vibes, walking bass
% 31-32 pop: band · 33-34 pixels: chip · 35-37 all at once: harp run, the motif in octaves, D major.
